    "content" : "RRS 270 Creativity; Decolonization; and Social Justice in Oceania (Units: 3)"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 101,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 34.333, 87.667, 296.333, 165.667 ],
    "font" : "Roboto-Regular",
    "font size" : 8.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0]",
    "content" : "on the stage, on ﬁlm, in community, in oratory, and in reading land, water, and environment. Introduction to the use of creative expression as a backbone of social justice and decolonization in Oceania. Focus on creative writing, literary studies, social justice, and diaspora in Oceania studies. Exploration of the ways Paciﬁc Islanders have organized and resisted colonialism through artistic practice and the power of the word."
  }, {
    "type" : "heading",
    "pdfua_tag" : "H1",
    "id" : 54,
    "level" : "Subtitle",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 310.667, 698.667, 556.667, 720.0 ],
    "heading level" : 1,
    "font" : "Roboto-Bold",
    "font size" : 8.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0]",
    "content" : "RRS 275 Introduction to Paciﬁc Islander Literature: How To Read An Ocean (Units: 3)"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 56,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 309.333, 598.333, 570.667, 699.0 ],
    "font" : "Roboto-Regular",
    "font size" : 8.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0]",
    "content" : "Examine Paciﬁc Islander writers and their histories of shaping terms and deﬁnitions of literature within Oceania as a region and beyond. Explore Paciﬁc Islander narratives about the intersections of gender, sexuality, race, colonialism, resistance, sovereignty, climate change, and understandings of connection to the environment through a wide range of reading materials, including novels, short stories, poetry, creative nonﬁction, and academic essays. Emphasis on the ways in which Paciﬁc Islander literatures shape complex and interconnected reflections of Oceania, ultimately speaking to the power of storytelling. Course Attributes:"
  }, {
